# `items`

`sisu doc` on a single file (decision 258): a page with every kind of
item. A single file shows everything, `pub` or not; its tests and its
`@cfg(test)` helpers are left out, as `sisu build` leaves them out.

The `##!` lines are the page's introduction, as Markdown.

## Contents

- [`Point`](#Point): A point in the plane.
- [`Counter`](#Counter): A counter that never goes above its limit.
- [`Shape`](#Shape): The shapes there are.
- [`ShapeError`](#ShapeError): What reading a shape can go wrong with.
- [`Area`](#Area): Something with an area.
- [`MAX_SHAPES`](#MAX_SHAPES): The most shapes a drawing holds.
- [`Drawing`](#Drawing): A drawing's shapes.
- [`Size`](#Size): A size that is never negative.
- [`parse`](#parse): Reads a shape from its name.
- [`save`](#save): Draws a drawing to a file.
- [`Studio`](#Studio): What a drawing needs from the world.
- [`open`](#open): Opens a studio.
- [`load`](#load): Reads a drawing back through any file system.
- [`scale`](#scale): Not finished yet.

<a id="Point"></a>
## `Point`

```sisu
@derive(Eq)
struct Point
    ## Across.
    x: int
    ## Up, zero unless given.
    y: int = 0
    ## The origin.
    const ORIGIN: Point

impl Display for Point
impl Point
```

A point in the plane.

Two points are equal when their coordinates are.

<a id="Point.steps"></a>
### `Point.steps`

```sisu
def steps(self, other: Point) -> int
```

The distance to `other`, in steps along the axes.

```sisu
assert Point(x=1, y=2).steps(Point(x=4, y=6)) == 7
```

<a id="Point.moved"></a>
### `Point.moved`

```sisu
def moved(self, dx: int) -> Point
```

The point moved by `dx` across.

<a id="Counter"></a>
## `Counter`

```sisu
struct Counter
    count: int
    limit: int
    invariant 0 <= self.count <= self.limit
```

A counter that never goes above its limit.

<a id="Counter.bump"></a>
### `Counter.bump`

```sisu
def bump(mut self) -> bool
    ensures self.count <= self.limit
    # re-checks the invariant of `Counter` on return
```

Counts one more, up to the limit.

<a id="Shape"></a>
## `Shape`

```sisu
@derive(Eq)
enum Shape
    ## A circle around the origin.
    Circle(radius: int)
    Square(side: int)

impl Area for Shape
```

The shapes there are.

<a id="ShapeError"></a>
## `ShapeError`

```sisu
@derive(Eq)
error ShapeError
    Empty
    Unknown(name: String)
    ..
```

What reading a shape can go wrong with.

<a id="Area"></a>
## `Area`

```sisu
trait Area
    ## The unit the area is in.
    type Unit
```

Something with an area.

<a id="Area.area"></a>
### `Area.area`

```sisu
def area(self) -> int
```

The area.

<a id="Area.is_empty"></a>
### `Area.is_empty`

```sisu
def is_empty(self) -> bool
```

Whether there is no area at all.

<a id="MAX_SHAPES"></a>
## `MAX_SHAPES`

```sisu
const MAX_SHAPES: int
```

The most shapes a drawing holds.

<a id="Drawing"></a>
## `Drawing`

```sisu
type Drawing = list[Shape]
```

A drawing's shapes.

<a id="Size"></a>
## `Size`

```sisu
type Size = int where self >= 0
    def try_from(value: int) -> Size ! RefinementError
```

A size that is never negative.

<a id="parse"></a>
## `parse`

```sisu
def parse(text: str) -> Shape ! ShapeError  # inferred
    requires len(text) < 100
```

Reads a shape from its name.

The names are those `Shape` has, in lower case:

```text
circle 3
square 2
```

```sisu
assert parse("circle 2") == Ok(Circle(2))
```

<a id="save"></a>
## `save`

```sisu
def save(fs: Fs, drawing: Drawing, path: Path) -> ! IoError
```

Draws a drawing to a file.

Capabilities: `fs` (`Fs`).

<a id="Studio"></a>
## `Studio`

```sisu
struct Studio
    fs: Fs
    clock: Clock
```

What a drawing needs from the world.

<a id="open"></a>
## `open`

```sisu
def open(studio: Studio, name: str, wait: Duration)
```

Opens a studio.

Capabilities: `studio` (`Fs`, `Clock`).

<a id="load"></a>
## `load`

```sisu
def load[F: FsOps](fs: F, path: Path) -> Drawing ! {IoError, ShapeError}  # inferred
```

Reads a drawing back through any file system.

Capabilities: `fs` (`Fs`).

